WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.140
The notch from the last
lesson is live on every call,

2
00:00:03.160 --> 00:00:04.380
and the whine at two thousand hertz

3
00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:05.120
is gone.

4
00:00:05.240 --> 00:00:06.440
Then new tickets arrive.

5
00:00:06.460 --> 00:00:08.780
Every time a call connects,
I hear a little tink,

6
00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:10.380
like someone tapped a tiny bell.

7
00:00:11.030 --> 00:00:12.850
Calls start with a relay click.

8
00:00:12.910 --> 00:00:14.570
A click should light every tone a little,

9
00:00:14.590 --> 00:00:16.390
a flat line on the frequency meter.

10
00:00:16.550 --> 00:00:19.450
Instead the meter shows one thin spike,
at two thousand hertz.

11
00:00:19.650 --> 00:00:22.750
The filter whose whole job is removing
two thousand hertz is making it.

12
00:00:23.770 --> 00:00:25.110
Do what lesson two taught.

13
00:00:25.130 --> 00:00:27.910
Send one click through the notch
and record what comes back.

14
00:00:28.130 --> 00:00:30.323
Point nine oh five, then zero,
point one seven two,

15
00:00:30.437 --> 00:00:32.110
zero, minus point one three nine.

16
00:00:32.130 --> 00:00:33.610
The click lasts one sample.

17
00:00:33.630 --> 00:00:34.650
The output keeps going.

18
00:00:34.670 --> 00:00:35.430
That's feedback.

19
00:00:35.930 --> 00:00:37.450
Up, nothing, down, nothing.

20
00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:39.710
That's a dot turning ninety
degrees per sample,

21
00:00:39.730 --> 00:00:41.130
which is two thousand hertz.

22
00:00:41.150 --> 00:00:41.870
There's the tink.

23
00:00:41.890 --> 00:00:43.970
Over two samples the ring
keeps point eight one,

24
00:00:43.990 --> 00:00:46.350
so point nine per sample,
the poles' radius.

25
00:00:47.120 --> 00:00:49.560
Now take the wheel,
and after every ninety degree turn,

26
00:00:49.580 --> 00:00:50.960
shrink the dot to point nine.

27
00:00:50.980 --> 00:00:51.880
It spirals in.

28
00:00:51.900 --> 00:00:54.220
Its shadow, the left-right position,
swings up, nothing,

29
00:00:54.240 --> 00:00:56.040
down, nothing, smaller each time.

30
00:00:56.060 --> 00:00:57.180
The turn sets the pitch.

31
00:00:57.200 --> 00:00:58.760
The shrink sets how fast it dies.

32
00:00:58.780 --> 00:01:00.600
That spiral is a pole, in time.

33
00:01:01.560 --> 00:01:04.980
The decay time is how long the ring takes
to shrink to one percent of where it

34
00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:05.660
started.

35
00:01:05.800 --> 00:01:08.460
Radius point nine gives
five and a half milliseconds.

36
00:01:08.680 --> 00:01:10.280
Point nine eight gives
twenty-eight and a half,

37
00:01:10.300 --> 00:01:11.600
five times as long.

38
00:01:11.660 --> 00:01:13.080
Halve the gap from pole to circle,

39
00:01:13.100 --> 00:01:14.560
and the decay time doubles.

40
00:01:15.220 --> 00:01:17.280
Closer poles make the notch narrower.

41
00:01:17.400 --> 00:01:18.760
The bandwidth is the width of the notch,

42
00:01:18.780 --> 00:01:21.930
in hertz, between the two tones on
either side that it passes at seventy-one

43
00:01:21.950 --> 00:01:22.440
percent.

44
00:01:22.920 --> 00:01:25.640
Radius point nine gives
two hundred sixty-six hertz.

45
00:01:25.740 --> 00:01:27.220
Point nine eight gives fifty-one.

46
00:01:27.240 --> 00:01:28.540
Bandwidth times decay time,

47
00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:30.880
in seconds, stays near one point four six.

48
00:01:32.090 --> 00:01:33.150
Why that number?

49
00:01:33.290 --> 00:01:34.970
The notch is a click minus a ring.

50
00:01:35.010 --> 00:01:36.710
In tones, a click is a flat line.

51
00:01:36.770 --> 00:01:38.950
The ring is a narrow peak
at two thousand hertz.

52
00:01:39.010 --> 00:01:41.310
Take it away,
and you've bitten two thousand hertz out.

53
00:01:41.730 --> 00:01:43.230
The ring is how the notch works.

54
00:01:43.250 --> 00:01:44.670
A narrow bite needs a narrow peak,

55
00:01:44.690 --> 00:01:46.570
and a narrow peak needs a long ring.

56
00:01:47.790 --> 00:01:51.350
The support lead wants the ring under
one percent within four milliseconds,

57
00:01:51.370 --> 00:01:53.650
and eighteen hundred hertz
kept at ninety percent.

58
00:01:53.890 --> 00:01:56.010
On the curve, no notch meets both.

59
00:01:56.110 --> 00:01:57.810
The lead settles for fifteen hundred.

60
00:01:57.930 --> 00:01:59.690
You ship radius point eight five.

61
00:01:59.750 --> 00:02:01.870
The ring fades
in three and a half milliseconds,

62
00:02:01.890 --> 00:02:03.890
and fifteen hundred keeps
ninety-three percent.

63
00:02:05.020 --> 00:02:06.540
No patch removes the tink.

64
00:02:06.560 --> 00:02:08.100
The ring cancels a steady whine.

65
00:02:08.120 --> 00:02:09.360
After a click, it rings alone.

66
00:02:09.380 --> 00:02:10.440
You only choose its length.

67
00:02:10.460 --> 00:02:12.200
Now it hides in the relay's click.

68
00:02:12.500 --> 00:02:14.040
Then a fax customer calls.

69
00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:15.720
Its tones arrive loud, but smeared.

70
00:02:15.740 --> 00:02:16.800
Something is too late.
